# What DVC must not walk.
#
# This was the stock template - three comment lines and no patterns - which means every `dvc
# status`, `dvc repro` and `dvc add` walked the whole working tree, including `.venv/`,
# `mlruns/`, every `__pycache__` and the 1.3 GB of checkpoints under `experiments/`. On this
# repo that is the difference between a status that answers and one you wait for.
#
# The rule for what belongs here: anything DVC could not be tracking, or that is regenerable
# from something it *is* tracking. Anything DVC tracks must NOT be listed, or it becomes
# invisible to the stage that declares it as an output.

# Environments and caches - never tracked, always large.
.venv/
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Regenerable from the artefacts DVC does track.
mlruns/
data/interim/pipeline_cache/

# Deliberately NOT listed: anything under `experiments/detect/`, `experiments/ocr/` or
# `experiments/llm/`. Three DVC stages declare whole directories there as outputs
# (`experiments/detect/final`, `experiments/detect/arrows/pose_m`, `experiments/ocr/trocr_large`),
# and every one of them contains `weights/last.pt`. Ignoring a file inside a tracked directory
# removes it from that directory's hash, which reports the output as modified and re-pushes it -
# the opposite of the saving this file is for.
